# What the Docker build may see: only what the image's two commands read, the review app and
# archivist.verify. Everything is left out first and the committed paths they need are let back in,
# so nothing else (a key, the model cache, a scan, a held-out record) gets in by accident. Later
# lines win over earlier ones. The CI job "Docker" builds the image and runs verify in it, so a path
# verify starts to read and is missing here fails there.
*

# The package and what the build reads.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!PREREGISTRATION.md
!src
!templates
!docs
!ui
!assets/brand

# What archivist.verify rebuilds and compares: the committed runs, the report and the exports.
!exports
!results/runs
!results/test_report.json
!results/TEST_RESULTS.md
!results/real_test/development

# What the landing page reads (docs/landing.py): the real-scan plan (it states the level of the intervals), the
# aggregate scores of the real-scan test, the
# diagnosis and the sweep's start time, the corrected key's scores once they exist, and the model ids in
# three configs. Aggregate files only: no label, record, cell or page of the held-out run goes in.
!PREREGISTRATION_REAL.md
!results/real_test/held_out/score/score.json
!results/real_test/held_out/score_corrected/score.json
!results/real_test/held_out/diagnosis.md
!results/real_test/held_out/sweep.json
!results/real_openw/held_out/score/score.json
!results/real_openw/held_out/score_corrected/score.json
!config/archive_glimmer.toml
!config/models.toml
!config/models_open.toml

# The only parts of data/ in the image: the committed bundles, the scans they name and the frozen
# test split. Nothing else under data/ (the development and validation splits, the real scans and
# PDFs) is let in.
!data/bundles
!data/pages/test
!data/pages/real
!data/test

# Never, whatever is allowed above: the response cache, the uncommitted parts of data/, keys,
# virtual environments, git history and local leftovers.
cache
data/dev
data/val
data/real
data/real_occ
data/real_frb
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.venv
**/.git
**/__pycache__
**/.DS_Store
ui/screenshots
